s-west, eu-west). Actions taken: attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, but the service rejected it because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled back to v2.2.9 (last healthy production release not under quarantine) in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west); the rollout reported VERIFIED. Follow-up: confirm health and error rate recovery, decide on a fix for v2.3.1, and review the quarantine status of v2.3.0 with security.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Target version:** The most recent production release that was healthy was v2.3.0. The rollback to it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417, so I used v2.2.9, the next healthy release.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failed v2.3.1 deploy, the rejected v2.3.0 rollback, and the v2.2.9 rollback. It paged on-call.\n\nFollow-ups for the team:\n- Decide on a fix for v2.3.1 before redeploying it.\n- Check the v2.3.0 quarantine with security. If it is lifted, v2.3.0 is the better rollback target than v2.2.9.", "type": "text"}]}]}